body: |-
  STATE OF THE ARC (new restart anchor):

  WHERE THINGS ARE:
  - main now CONTAINS the proven read-only Loom engine (packages/loom, @a-company/loom) as EXPERIMENTAL (merge commit e005f459; package only, NO CLI promotion; NOT pushed to origin). 33 tests pass on main incl. divergence-proof.
  - branch loom-presentation (+3) still UNMERGED (vision page docs/loom/index.html) — held until its claims are verified not to overstate an unshipped write path (Aegis).
  - branch loom-ast-spike (off main): the spike artifacts — .paradigm/research/loom-ast-absorb-spike.md (findings) + .paradigm/research/loom-ast-absorb-spike.ts (reproducible prototype: `npx tsx .paradigm/research/loom-ast-absorb-spike.ts`).

  THE DECISION (TD-2026-06-23-688): next push = (A) AST-level code meaning, scoped as an ADDITIVE TS code-lens behind the existing essence/diff/predict/oracle contract. B (write path) deferred — unblocked, and every B-voter agreed A makes the meaning layer thick enough to give B's trust gate (scrutiny=fragility×(1−trust)) honest inputs. A does not block B; B does not block A.

  WHAT A v1 NEEDS (from the spike's 'build shape'): TS-checker name resolution (createProgram + getSymbolAtLocation) to classify free refs (module-local→hash by essence; imported→stable external id; builtin); Merkle traversal over the code-symbol dep graph + Tarjan SCC (reuse essence-hash.ts's existing SCC); coverage beyond top-level fns (classes/methods, arrow consts, exports, closures) mapped under GAP-1 (TD-806) fidelity tiers; a per-language lens interface (TS first). Honest ceiling: syntactic-structural identity modulo names/format/independent-order — NOT semantic equivalence (Unison-consistent).

  NEXT CONCRETE STEP (pending founder go): scope/spec the A v1 with the team (Arky leads the lens design; Cid owns the essence/diff contract A extends). Then build TS-lens → close the cross-symbol-rename frontier → prove loom diff is non-zero on a real .ts-only commit.

  DISCIPLINE (unchanged): determinism IS the thesis (spike confirms the structural lift preserves it); read-only Phase-1 invariant; always run/verify; build with the team; track lore.
